# What is committed is LF. This repo is the tree's worst case for line endings:
# capture.sh runs on macOS, where a CRLF shell script fails with an error that
# names nothing useful, and `core.autocrlf` is `true` on the Windows dev box and
# does NOT normalise on the way in (see the root CLAUDE.md, which documents CRLF
# blobs reaching origin twice). Unlike the other repos here, this one states the
# intent AND enforces it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed or parsed by macOS toolchains. A CR in any of these is a build break,
# not a cosmetic diff.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.swift     text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.plist     text eol=lf
*.entitlements text eol=lf
*.pbxproj   text eol=lf
*.xcscheme  text eol=lf
*.storyboard text eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched.
*.png       binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.ico       binary
